---
import ArticleLayout from '../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
---

<ArticleLayout
	title="Articles — Semantic Signal LLM Trader"
	description="Technical notes on the Semantic Signal engine: one analysis cycle, trade memory, order execution, how the numbers are produced, and one offline replay of recorded cycles."
	meta="Articles · October 2026"
>
	<span slot="title">Articles</span>
	<p slot="subtitle" class="subtitle">Notes on how the engine is built, what it stores, and how its numbers are produced. Each page names the repository path behind its claims.</p>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Technical notes</h2>

		<div class="article-card">
			<h3><a href="/articles/chart-vision/">One analysis cycle, step by step</a></h3>
			<p>Market data, indicators, the chart image, news, memory, the model call — and the checks that run after it, outside the prompt. <span class="date">October 2026</span></p>
		</div>

		<div class="article-card">
			<h3><a href="/articles/vector-memory/">Trade memory: what is stored and what is retrieved</a></h3>
			<p>Closed trades as 768-dimensional vectors in ChromaDB: three collections, the 3/20/3 retrieval rules, the surprise ratio, and why a dozen trades still count as anecdotes. <span class="date">October 2026</span></p>
		</div>

		<div class="article-card">
			<h3><a href="/articles/executor-separation/">Order execution as a separate service</a></h3>
			<p>Why the engine does not place its own orders, the seven checks in the executor, the verdict journal, and the state of the live path: testnet only, reconciliation still weak. <span class="date">October 2026</span></p>
		</div>

		<div class="article-card">
			<h3><a href="/articles/measurement/">Where the numbers come from</a></h3>
			<p>The paper ledger behind every performance figure on this site — window, 12 trades, inference cost, buy-and-hold comparison — and the gaps (zero fees, tiny sample) that keep it from being evidence. <span class="date">October 2026</span></p>
		</div>

		<div class="article-card">
			<h3><a href="/articles/offline-replay/">Replaying 55 historical setups: one comparison</a></h3>
			<p>The bot's own recorded cycles replayed through two prompt versions and two model generations: what changed, what matched, and why a replay without outcomes cannot rank the variants. <span class="date">October 2026</span></p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<h2>Longer reads</h2>

		<div class="article-card">
			<h3><a href="/story/">The development story (December 2025 – September 2026)</a></h3>
			<p>How the engine changed phase by phase, with commit dates, the mathematics behind the gates, a status report and a list of claims this site got wrong and had to fix. <span class="date">September 2026</span></p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<div class="cta-box">
		<p>The live dashboard shows the current position, the latest prompt and the decision behind it.</p>
		<a href="https://semanticsignal.qrak.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">Live dashboard ↗</a>
		<a href="https://github.com/qrak/LLM_trader" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-secondary">GitHub ↗</a>
	</div>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
	.article-card {
		background: var(--bg-card);
		border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
		border-radius: 10px;
		padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
		transition: border-color 0.2s ease;
	}

	.article-card:hover {
		border-color: var(--border-accent);
	}

	.article-card h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
	}

	.article-card h3 a {
		color: var(--text-main);
	}

	.article-card h3 a:hover {
		color: var(--accent-emerald);
	}

	.article-card p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.98rem;
	}

	.article-card .date {
		color: var(--text-dim);
		font-size: 0.85em;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
</style>
